{"authored" [{"question" "q-161729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,2\\le y\\le 2xz}.\n$$\n\nFor a fixed admissible $x$, let $[a(x),b(x)]$ be the full nonempty $z$ fiber of the exactly specified region $S$. Use ordered inner bounds and the actual outer $x$ range. What is $a(x)\\times b(x)$?" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161729/review.json" "file_sha256" "b0bb2046e7b22a6212a1ddfed335a93ba90900c86081d95a47a6e7ffd4e3c19d" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161729/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "1d1dcee46ca4ab1c3c89619b57b7109271c63246bee4294251b495d11dda7c65" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161729/verification.json" "basis" 2080 "rationale" "Retain exact S; source nominal key0 differs from actual nonempty fiber product2. Replace only the changed field component, keeping existing answer2 and all other answer identities."} {"question" "q-161729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $S$ is retained exactly. A nonempty $y$ fiber requires $2\\le2xz$, so $xz\\ge1$. The inequality $0\\le z\\le2x$ then forces $x>0$. For a fixed admissible $x$, combine these requirements to obtain\n\n$$\\frac1x\\le z\\le2x.$$\n\nThis interval is nonempty precisely when $1/x\\le2x$, giving $1/\\sqrt2\\le x\\le2$. Every point in this base admits $2\\le y\\le2xz$. Thus the full nonempty $z$ fiber has endpoints $a(x)=1/x$ and $b(x)=2x$, with\n\n$$a(x)b(x)=\\frac1x(2x)=2.$$\n\nThe valid repeated integral is\n\n$$\\iiint_S f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\int_{1/\\sqrt2}^{2}\\int_{1/x}^{2x}\\int_2^{2xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.$$\n\nFor $f=1$, integrating in $y$ and $z$ gives $4x^3-4x+1/x$, hence the volume is\n\n$$[x^4-2x^2+\\ln x]_{1/\\sqrt2}^{2}=\\frac{35}{4}+\\frac32\\ln2>0.$$\n\nThe authentic source solution copied the nominal pair $0,2x$ and reported its product $0$. Its formal repeated integral over $x\\in[-2,2]$ includes reversed and empty fibers; for $f=1$ it gives $0$, not the volume of $S$. The full nonempty fiber has endpoint product $2$." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161729/review.json" "file_sha256" "b0bb2046e7b22a6212a1ddfed335a93ba90900c86081d95a47a6e7ffd4e3c19d" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161729/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "1d1dcee46ca4ab1c3c89619b57b7109271c63246bee4294251b495d11dda7c65" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161729/verification.json" "basis" 2080 "rationale" "Retain exact S; source nominal key0 differs from actual nonempty fiber product2. Replace only the changed field component, keeping existing answer2 and all other answer identities."} {"question" "q-161729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161729/review.json" "file_sha256" "b0bb2046e7b22a6212a1ddfed335a93ba90900c86081d95a47a6e7ffd4e3c19d" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161729/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "1d1dcee46ca4ab1c3c89619b57b7109271c63246bee4294251b495d11dda7c65" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161729/verification.json" "basis" 2080 "rationale" "Retain exact S; source nominal key0 differs from actual nonempty fiber product2. Replace only the changed field component, keeping existing answer2 and all other answer identities."} {"question" "q-161729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,2\\le y\\le 2xz}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a\\times b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/state.json" "file_sha256" "788a9691568f64cb7c13aa285ad76c93e87db7b16a06c4ae123e8caa4136a543" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=2,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)=2xz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{2}^{2xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}[{\\int }_{2}^{2xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}{\\int }_{2}^{2xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na\\times b=(0)\\times (2x)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/state.json" "file_sha256" "788a9691568f64cb7c13aa285ad76c93e87db7b16a06c4ae123e8caa4136a543" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "27b5b7a888138e758a90a755e287632e41cbd828d2ec0cea0caf31069fdb088a" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-161729" []} "basis" 2080 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186347067 17592186347068 17592186347069 17592186347070 17592186347071] "immutable_fields" [[17592186347166 :answer-field/correct] [17592186347166 :answer-field/id] [17592186347166 :answer-field/key] [17592186347166 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
